## V0 Policy Surface

The v0 compiler selects exactly one next experiment. It does not flatten the
five decision axes into a weighted scalar. It uses one declared lexicographic
policy:

```text
information-first    = information, falsification, divergence, lower risk, lower cost
falsification-first  = falsification, information, divergence, lower risk, lower cost
counterfactual-first = divergence, falsification, information, lower risk, lower cost
```

Candidate ID is the final stable tie-break. Candidates exceeding the integer
budget are infeasible. Every selected candidate is checked against every
feasible rival by the native Sounio rule `attention_selected_not_dominated`.
The full canonical candidate set is retained inside the hash-chained worldline,
so replay recomputes the decision rather than trusting the selected ID.

The selected event is also the resource reservation. Completion consumes that
live reservation and binds a nonzero outcome digest. This removes the crash
window between a scheduling receipt and a separate capability-acquire event.

## Integration Receipt

The executable v0 receipt is
`tools/loom/evidence/loom-attention-compiler-v0-20260826.txt`. It records the
linear Sounio typestate diagnostics, exact-frame comparator sabotage, three
different policy selections, bidirectional exclusion between attention plans
and ordinary capabilities, completion-bound release, canonical replay,
journal/Arrow sabotage, full Loom crash recovery, Provider ABI regression, and
atomic shared-runtime install/upgrade/rollback test. These observations support
only the bounded claim above.

## Falsification Conditions

- a selected candidate differs from deterministic replay of its canonical set;
- any feasible rival dominates the selected candidate under the named policy;
- removing only `attention_selected_not_dominated` does not admit the exact
  otherwise-refused dominated pair;
- a candidate targets a world or claim absent from verified worldlines;
- a selected experiment exceeds its declared budget;
- two live plans or capabilities reserve the same exact resource;
- completion changes owner or generation, or omits an outcome digest;
- a mutated attention event contributes an Arrow row;
- a UI, Arrow table, model response, or provider CLI becomes scheduling
  authority.
